MOUNTPROBE(1)

NAME
    mountprobe - exercise SmallOS mount-table and statfs compatibility

SYNOPSIS
    mountprobe

DESCRIPTION
    mountprobe validates the kernel-backed static mount table for the ext2
    root filesystem, /proc, and /dev. It checks /proc/mounts output, statfs
    and fstatfs filesystem identities, unsupported mount failures, and busy
    unmount failures for the pinned static mounts.

    This probe intentionally documents the current mount milestone boundary:
    dynamic VFS stacking is not enabled yet, so supported filesystem types on
    otherwise valid new mount points fail with ENOSYS.
